# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rowan — environment configuration example
#
# Usage:
#   cp .env.example .env.local      # local development
#
# `.env.local` and every other `.env*` file except this one are git-ignored.
# Never commit real credentials.
#
# Phase 1 requires no secrets: the application shell renders with an empty
# environment, and neither a database nor an AI provider key is needed.
# Database and provider variables are introduced in Phase 2 and Phase 3.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Public origin of the deployment, used to build absolute URLs (metadata).
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are embedded in the browser bundle: never put a secret here.
# Optional today — when unset, metadata falls back to relative URLs.
#
#   Local development : http://localhost:3000
#   Preview           : the preview deployment URL Vercel assigns
#   Production        : https://your-production-domain
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://rowan.example.com

# Minimum level emitted by the server-side structured logger.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One of: debug | info | warn | error. Defaults to "info".
# Server-only; it is never sent to the browser.
#
# LOG_LEVEL=info
